## What this part does

Task 1.G3 is a run, not a code change. The run needs data from two databases, and the adapter does not
read a secret and does not start a proxy. So part 1 prepares the tools that Daniel runs.
Task 1.G3 stays `[ ]`. No task turns `[x]` or `[b]`.

Three new files, all in the track's runs folder:

1. `measure/runs/levels_5_9_20261006/g3-crosscheck.ts` is the read-only cross-check. It reads the passages
   inventory and `MONOREPO_DATABASE_URL`. It sets `default_transaction_read_only`, opens `BEGIN READ ONLY`,
   and rolls back. Every query passes `isReadOnlySql`. Through `primary_legacy_id_map` it finds the monorepo
   row of each level 5-9 legacy article. It writes the counts on both sides, the ids on one side only, and the
   differing ids with the monorepo text. A differing id takes the monorepo `title`, `summary`, and `passage`
   in a merged inventory next to the `--out` file. The report holds counts and ids only.

2. `measure/runs/levels_5_9_20261006/g3-daniel-run.sh` is Daniel's run. It makes the handoff folder outside
   git, starts the Cloud SQL proxy on 127.0.0.1:5433, waits for the port, and stops the proxy on exit. It runs
   `inventory-legacy.ts --levels 5,6,7,8,9`, then the cross-check. It prints counts, paths, and exit codes
   only. It writes nothing inside the Workbooks git tree.

3. `measure/runs/levels_5_9_20261006/g3-prep-tsc.txt` holds the tsc check: exit 0, no output line.

Monorepo table and column names, from the schema files of `../reading-advantage-monorepo` (read only):

- `articles`, `packages/db/src/schema/content.ts` line 8. Columns `title` (10), `summary` (12), `level` (13),
  `passage` (22). `ra_level` (26) holds the same legacy value: the ETL writes the legacy `ra_level` into both
  `level` and `ra_level` (`packages/db/src/migrations-data/primary-legacy-import.ts` lines 289, 301).
- `primary_legacy_id_map`, `packages/db/src/schema/primary.ts` line 249. Columns `table_name` (251),
  `legacy_id` (252), `new_id` (253). The `article` rows map the legacy cuid to `articles.id`.

Connection names, both confirmed in the monorepo docs:

- legacy: secret `DATABASE_URL`, project `primary-advantage`, database `primary_advantage`
  (`docs/content-plans/primary-db-field-map.md`).
- monorepo: secret `PRIMARY_V2_DATABASE_URL`, version 1, project `primary-advantage`, database `primary_v2`
  (`../reading-advantage-monorepo/docs/deployment/tutor-switch-brief.md` line 55;
  `primary-cutover-migration-spec.md` line 136 pins version 1).
- instance `reading-advantage:asia-southeast1:cloud-sql` for both.

A bare `pg` import cannot resolve from `measure/`, because `dashboard/node_modules` is not a parent folder of
the file. The script loads `pg` through `createRequire` on `dashboard/package.json`, anchored on the script's
own path. No environment variable is needed for module resolution.

## Checks (no database, no secret)

1. tsc: `cd dashboard && npx tsc --noEmit --skipLibCheck --esModuleInterop --module nodenext
   --moduleResolution nodenext --target es2022 ../measure/runs/levels_5_9_20261006/g3-crosscheck.ts`
   exits 0 with no output line. Capture `g3-prep-tsc.txt`.
2. `bash -n measure/runs/levels_5_9_20261006/g3-daniel-run.sh` exits 0.
3. Dry call with no `MONOREPO_DATABASE_URL` exits 2, prints `Set MONOREPO_DATABASE_URL to the database URL`,
   and prints no URL.
4. `grep` on both files finds no URL and no password. The only `secret` words name the secret, not its value.
5. Logic probe, outside the repo in `/tmp/opencode`: a trimmed compare matches equal text with padding, and
   lists a title-only difference. A passage difference replaces the text and recomputes `words` (3 to 4). The
   crosscheck JSON holds basenames only. The report holds no passage text. The probe caught one defect before
   the commit: `crossCheck` copied a caller path into `mergedInventory`. It now takes `path.basename` itself.

## What part 2 waits for

Daniel runs `bash measure/runs/levels_5_9_20261006/g3-daniel-run.sh`. Then he copies
`~/Desktop/handoff/levels-5-9-passages-2026-11-19/g3-crosscheck.txt` to
`measure/runs/levels_5_9_20261006/g3-crosscheck.txt`. The merged inventory is the `--inventory` input of the
plan's heavy-run, and its counts and keep counts go to `g3-run.txt`.

